articles.content_en:
Article 1 An Intellectual Property Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance cases within the urban area of the city where it is located:
(1) civil and administrative cases involving patents, new plant varieties, layout designs of integrated circuits, technical secrets, and computer software;
(2) administrative cases where prosecution is brought against administrative actions involving copyright, trademarks, unfair competition, etc., taken by departments of the State Council or local people's governments at or above the county level;
(3) civil cases involving the recognition of well-known trademarks.

Article 5 The Beijing Intellectual Property Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance administrative cases:
(1) cases against the rulings or decisions on the authorization and confirmation of intellectual property rights concerning patents, trademarks, new plant varieties, layout designs of integrated circuits, etc., made by departments of the State Council;
(2) cases against the decisions on compulsory licensing, and the adjudications on the fees or remuneration for compulsory licensing, concerning patents, new plant varieties, and layout designs of integrated circuits, made by departments of the State Council;
(3) cases against other administrative actions involving the authorization and confirmation of intellectual property rights made by departments of the State Council.
